# S-II ullage motor (on the S-IC/S-II interstage): NASA CEA input deck (RP-1311 free form).
# Run by tools/make_exhaust_table.py; the spec takes the equilibrium
# expansion (a frozen one stops at the throat: its condensed species
# leave their temperature ranges).
#
# Propellant: ammonium perchlorate 82 % of its weight (MSFC-MAN-503 p. 5-24,
#   H); the other 18 % is taken as TP-E-8104's other ingredients in their
#   proportions (L).
# p,psia: 999, the eight AS-501 motors' mean burn-time chamber pressure
#   (AS-501 FER Table 12-3, H; limits 900-1,075).
# supar: 7.5 (L): the area ratio at which this deck's vacuum thrust
#   coefficient puts the exit of a nozzle delivering 23,000 lbf
#   (MSFC-MAN-506) at 0.9 of the 12.5 in case (MSFC-MAN-503 p. 5-24).
# Propellant: Thiokol TP-E-8104, polysulfide (LP-33) and ammonium
#   perchlorate with 2 % aluminium, by weight (TN D-6295 Table I(a), H). The
#   heats of formation not in CEA's library are the deck's: LP-33 per
#   C5H10O2S2 repeat unit -493 kJ/mol, set so that CEA gives TN D-6295 Table
#   I(b)'s flame temperature, 4,404 F (2,702 K) at 1,000 psia (its chamber
#   gamma then comes out at the table's 1.176, an independent check); GMF
#   (p-quinone dioxime) 0, dibutyl carbitol -640 and diphenylguanidine +140
#   kJ/mol, estimates (L; together 4 % of the mass). Benzyl mercaptan (0 to
#   0.09 %) is left out.
# omit: CEA 3.3.4's equilibrium expansion does not converge past the throat
#   with the spinel MgAl2O4 (0.5 mol % in the chamber), so its Mg and Al go
#   to MgO, MgCl2 and Al2O3.
reac
  fuel=NH4CLO4(I)                                    wt%=82.000 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=AL(cr)                                        wt%=1.286 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=LP-33      C 5 H 10 O 2 S 2 h,kj/mol=-493     wt%=12.092 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=GMF        C 6 H 6 N 2 O 2 h,kj/mol=0         wt%=0.894 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=S(a)                                          wt%=0.006 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=MgO(cr)                                       wt%=0.643 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=Fe2O3(cr)                                     wt%=1.286 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=TP-903     C 12 H 26 O 3 h,kj/mol=-640        wt%=1.344 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=DPG        C 13 H 13 N 3 h,kj/mol=140         wt%=0.450 t(k)=298.15
prob case=S-II-ullage rocket p,psia=999 eql supar=7.5
omit MgAL2O4(cr) MgAL2O4(L)
output siunits trace=1e-5
end
